Lab Material
Lab 15 - Monitor OpenStack Operations
Objectives
To monitor the operations and health of OpenStack components using open-source tools
To implement telemetry with Ceilometer, Gnocchi, and Monasca
To set up centralized logging with Elasticsearch-Fluentd-Kibana (EFK) stack
To configure Grafana for visualization and alerting
Prerequisites
OpenStack environment (minimum: Stein release)
Ubuntu 20.04 LTS or CentOS 8 nodes
sudo/root access to all nodes
Minimum hardware: 4 vCPUs, 8GB RAM, 50GB disk per node
Basic familiarity with Linux CLI and OpenStack concepts
Task 1: Set Up Ceilometer and Gnocchi for Telemetry
**Subtask 1.1: Install Ceilometer Components
# On controller node
sudo apt-get install ceilometer-api ceilometer-collector \
ceilometer-agent-central ceilometer-agent-notification \
python3-ceilometerclient
Subtask 1.2: Configure Ceilometer
# Edit the configuration file
sudo vi /etc/ceilometer/ceilometer.conf

# In the [DEFAULT] section add:
transport_url = rabbit://openstack:RABBIT_PASS@controller
auth_strategy = keystone

# In the [service_credentials] section:
auth_type = password
auth_url = http://controller:5000/v3
username = ceilometer
password = CEILOMETER_PASS
project_name = service
user_domain_name = Default
project_domain_name = Default
Subtask 1.3: Install and Configure Gnocchi
sudo apt-get install gnocchi-api gnocchi-metricd python3-gnocchiclient

# Configure Gnocchi
sudo vi /etc/gnocchi/gnocchi.conf

# Add these configurations:
[storage]
driver = file
file_basepath = /var/lib/gnocchi

[indexer]
url = mysql+pymysql://gnocchi:GNOCCHI_DBPASS@controller/gnocchi
Subtask 1.4: Start Services
sudo systemctl enable --now ceilometer-agent-central
sudo systemctl enable --now ceilometer-agent-notification
sudo systemctl enable --now ceilometer-api
sudo systemctl enable --now gnocchi-api
sudo systemctl enable --now gnocchi-metricd
Expected Outcome:

Ceilometer services running and collecting metrics
Gnocchi storing time-series data
Verify with openstack metric list
Task 2: Set Up Monasca for Advanced Monitoring
Subtask 2.1: Install Monasca Components
sudo apt-get install monasca-api monasca-notification \
monasca-persister monasca-agent
Subtask 2.2: Configure Monasca
sudo vi /etc/monasca/monasca-api.conf

# Add database configuration:
[database]
engine = mysql
host = controller
name = monasca
user = monasca
passwd = MONASCA_DBPASS
Subtask 2.3: Initialize Database
mysql -u root -p
CREATE DATABASE monasca;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON monasca.* TO 'monasca'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'MONASCA_DBPASS';
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
exit
Expected Outcome:

Monasca services operational
Verify with curl http://controller:8070/v2.0
Task 3: Implement EFK Stack for Logging
Subtask 3.1: Install Elasticsearch
wget -qO - https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch | sudo apt-key add -
echo "deb https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/7.x/apt stable main" | sudo tee -a /etc/apt/sources.list.d/elastic-7.x.list
sudo apt update && sudo apt install elasticsearch

# Configure Elasticsearch
sudo vi /etc/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.yml
cluster.name: openstack-logging
network.host: 0.0.0.0
Subtask 3.2: Install Fluentd
curl -L https://toolbelt.treasuredata.com/sh/install-ubuntu-focal-td-agent4.sh | sh
sudo /usr/sbin/td-agent-gem install fluent-plugin-elasticsearch
Subtask 3.3: Configure Fluentd
sudo vi /etc/td-agent/td-agent.conf

# Add this configuration:
<source>
  @type tail
  path /var/log/nova/*.log
  pos_file /var/log/td-agent/nova.log.pos
  tag openstack.nova
  <parse>
    @type none
  </parse>
</source>

<match openstack.**>
  @type elasticsearch
  host controller
  port 9200
  logstash_format true
</match>
Subtask 3.4: Install Kibana
sudo apt install kibana
sudo vi /etc/kibana/kibana.yml

# Set these parameters:
server.host: "0.0.0.0"
elasticsearch.hosts: ["http://controller:9200"]
Expected Outcome:

Logs visible in Kibana dashboard at http://controller:5601
Elasticsearch indices created for OpenStack services
Task 4: Configure Grafana for Visualization
Subtask 4.1: Install Grafana
sudo apt-get install -y apt-transport-https
sudo apt-get install -y software-properties-common wget
wget -q -O - https://packages.grafana.com/gpg.key | sudo apt-key add -
echo "deb https://packages.grafana.com/oss/deb stable main" | sudo tee -a /etc/apt/sources.list.d/grafana.list
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install grafana
Subtask 4.2: Configure Data Sources
# Access Grafana at http://controller:3000
# Add data sources:
1. Gnocchi (http://controller:8041)
2. Monasca (http://controller:8070/v2.0)
3. Elasticsearch (http://controller:9200)
